entry.content:
&lt;p&gt;atop mounds of sand,&lt;br /&gt;
pillars of smoke and iron&lt;br /&gt;
stand&lt;br /&gt;
lattices of falling leaves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;where little metal men slide up and down&lt;br /&gt;
along the grooves and grain, the sea&lt;br /&gt;
of fog and soot and wood&lt;br /&gt;
and piercing—&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;hexagons, basalt&lt;br /&gt;
from scorched,&lt;br /&gt;
assaulted earth&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and all across them&lt;br /&gt;
all along arrays&lt;br /&gt;
of pipes and pumps&lt;br /&gt;
there lay lines on lay lines&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;witches burn and trees rot:&lt;br /&gt;
silver and stone&lt;br /&gt;
to carbon and steel,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;clockwork alive and&lt;br /&gt;
infinitely high I—&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;the ground is gone now&lt;br /&gt;
and i cannot see the sky&lt;br /&gt;
nor fly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;so i climb&lt;br /&gt;
ducts down&lt;br /&gt;
polls up ladders and&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;try not to fall, just&lt;br /&gt;
a little longer&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;the fragile flower&lt;br /&gt;
—three days dead,&lt;br /&gt;
wilted red—&lt;br /&gt;
blooms through&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;the forest floor&lt;br /&gt;
of tight knit grass&lt;br /&gt;
—the narrow path—&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;push dew drops down,&lt;br /&gt;
back to the ground,&lt;br /&gt;
to the soil,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;as pollen sprays&lt;br /&gt;
and spreads on winds&lt;br /&gt;
out to the world&lt;br /&gt;
—the word.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;the flower is born once more&lt;br /&gt;
in the forest grey and brown&lt;br /&gt;
—which tore itself apart&lt;br /&gt;
in search of color—&lt;br /&gt;
next spring&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;watch—&lt;br /&gt;
the acorn drops,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;it cracks, splintered&lt;br /&gt;
against the august pavement&lt;br /&gt;
burnt black by the harsh&lt;br /&gt;
southern sun, summers past&lt;br /&gt;
since spalled and&lt;br /&gt;
hardened oil spilled&lt;br /&gt;
across the land&lt;br /&gt;
where ancient acorns&lt;br /&gt;
fell and grew.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;but the crow stares down,&lt;br /&gt;
its dark eyes indifferent&lt;br /&gt;
as engines roar below&lt;br /&gt;
and the acorn&lt;br /&gt;
is smashed to a pulp,&lt;br /&gt;
laid bare,&lt;br /&gt;
exposed to the crow,&lt;br /&gt;
which its ancestors&lt;br /&gt;
long ago conquered&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;a heavy blanket never slept&lt;br /&gt;
until the tip of night i wept&lt;br /&gt;
i climbed upon the blackthorn tree&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;em&gt;and cut a sweeter apple for thee&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;i have seen the best minds of my generation cowering in coffeehouses,&lt;br /&gt;
    cold brew burnt out of this world and pulled back through!&lt;br /&gt;
    rot consumed the wooden planks and knots that bind them are to blame?!&lt;br /&gt;
ecstasy! broken typists lay around us, endangered yet blindingly aware,&lt;br /&gt;
who trade ginger and sell roots while urban structures still stand&lt;br /&gt;
    purchase focus and forgetfulness,&lt;br /&gt;
    abstract freedom found in screens,&lt;br /&gt;
    owned by corpses of collective action and corporate board meetings&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;whose plugged in spirits burst and bubble with memory mappings and pointers to a void,&lt;br /&gt;
who work faster now—&lt;br /&gt;
    quiet screaming, number than before&lt;br /&gt;
    harmonizing with the other strung up souls&lt;br /&gt;
who revel in mechanical sanctity, divested of their own,&lt;br /&gt;
    dogs for the towers which shrewdly shelter them,&lt;br /&gt;
    laying bricks for the great mechanical edifice:&lt;br /&gt;
    a bridge to cross the rubicon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;who quench their fears with homegrown needles, hoping to hit arteries.&lt;br /&gt;
who forget secrets each day, meet again with each blackened sip and retold open lie.&lt;br /&gt;
who cling to shreds of liberalism, once discarded for red-black wet dreams&lt;br /&gt;
    raise up glasses by the ocean, watch meek waves lap&lt;br /&gt;
    against the cliffs of Oregon Country as the Great Lakes iced blue&lt;br /&gt;
who hide in the museum—words! words! at 22:50 AM—among the art called&lt;br /&gt;
    dolls to cynically hide the pain—yet in its promises and doubts art &lt;em&gt;will&lt;/em&gt; suffice!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;whose paranoid fits leave them backwards on chairs, facing broken cameras and torn up curtains,&lt;br /&gt;
    which once they called their only home, now screaming hysterically naked&lt;br /&gt;
    for no one or the world to see&lt;br /&gt;
who chew on bitter chalk, dry up, cease skinning thoughts, voice ripping fantasies.&lt;br /&gt;
who push it down their throats&lt;br /&gt;
    relish in the salt, cry at diltation and collapse.&lt;br /&gt;
who worship under the blinding, burning light, smoldering in chiaroscuro.&lt;br /&gt;
    godspurned screams to up to the sky&lt;br /&gt;
    wander one more forty years before He&#39;ll hear you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;who crave that queer, blessed unrest&lt;br /&gt;
    that humming, buzzing air that keeps them marching&lt;br /&gt;
    and makes them more alive than the others&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;who&lt;br /&gt;
    agony and terror forced through splintering wooden doors, into the cafe lights&lt;br /&gt;
    feel curse marks acrossed their necks—branded by doctors, lovers, and false gods&lt;br /&gt;
    yearn for her unclean, kosher body—born broken, piercing, demonettes—and can&#39;t bear it!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;who find themselves as failed men, deluded and reshaped.&lt;br /&gt;
who lean closer, weakening at the sight of her spindled hands&lt;br /&gt;
    grazing their tattooed freckles—basilisk bug—to be crumbled by its emerging eyespots&lt;br /&gt;
    as whispered ballads, two-part soliloquies of ecstasy through hours lived and slept&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;who walk onto grass, away from the light&lt;br /&gt;
    find the deepest darkness between buildings&lt;br /&gt;
who arch their backs, held yet closer through,&lt;br /&gt;
    shrieking and moaning&lt;br /&gt;
    pierced by silver and peachwood&lt;br /&gt;
    squeezing chitin and porcelain&lt;br /&gt;
    rend the flesh from their skin&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;who twirl and pretend, gaze longingly, skating down cobbled streets&lt;br /&gt;
    to find themselves at train stops,&lt;br /&gt;
    with dreams of wildflowers and rusted boats&lt;/p&gt;
